extends layout

block config
  - bodyClass = 'lab-app'

block extra_css
  link(rel='stylesheet', href='/stylesheets/lab-theme.css?v=p3fix1')
  style.
    .attack-sim { max-width: 1040px; margin: 0 auto; }
    .attack-sim .lab-landing__brand h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem); }
    .attack-table-wrap table { margin-bottom: 0; min-width: 720px; }
    .attack-sim .help-block { color: #5c7380; margin-top: 6px; margin-bottom: 0; }
    .attack-sim .panel { margin-bottom: 18px; }
    #simStatus { color: #5c7380; margin: 12px 0 0; min-height: 1.2em; }
    .attack-chart { margin-top: 8px; }
    .attack-chart__row {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 4.5rem 1fr 4.5rem;
      gap: 10px;
      align-items: center;
      margin: 8px 0;
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    }
    .attack-chart__track {
      height: 14px;
      background: rgba(15, 28, 36, 0.06);
      border-radius: 999px;
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    .attack-chart__bar {
      height: 100%;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, #0f766e, #14b8a6);
      border-radius: 999px;
    }
    .attack-table-wrap {
      max-height: 32rem;
      overflow: auto;
      border: 1px solid rgba(15, 28, 36, 0.08);
      border-radius: 12px;
    }
    .attack-table-wrap thead th {
      position: sticky;
      top: 0;
      background: #f7fbfb;
      z-index: 1;
    }
    .attack-result--win { color: #0f766e; font-weight: 700; }
    .attack-result--fail { color: #c2410c; font-weight: 700; }
    .attack-sim details { margin-top: 12px; color: #2a3d4a; }
    .attack-sim details summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; }

block content
  .container.attack-sim#attack-sim
    .lab-landing__brand
      span.lab-landing__eyebrow Classroom tool
      h1 51% Attack Simulator
      p.lead
        | Race a private chain against honest miners. Each next block is random.
        | The attacker finds it with probability equal to their hash share.

    .lab-about
      h3 What you are watching
      p
        | An attacker spends their hash power on a private chain that starts 1, 2, or 3 blocks behind the public tip. Honest miners keep extending the public chain. The classroom hub follows the longer chain. When the private chain grows longer, the hub switches to it. That switch is a reorganization, and the attack wins.
      p
        | Every block is a weighted coin flip. The attacker finds the next block with probability equal to their share of the hash power, and an honest miner finds it otherwise. A 30% attacker wins some races. A 70% attacker loses some. This page never picks the winner in advance. Leave the seed blank to use the browser’s Math.random, or enter a seed to replay the same luck.
      p
        | Each trial uses the lab’s real hub code:
        |
        code tryAddBlock
        |  and
        |
        code _selectBestChain
        |  in RelayBlockchainState. The longest chain wins, and a tie stays with the chain the hub saw first. The hub also rejects a block whose parent is more than 10 blocks behind the current tip, so a phone that fell asleep cannot flood the class with old work. For an attacker that rule is final. Once their private tip is 11 blocks behind, the next private block is rejected and they cannot catch up. Give-up depth defaults to 11 so a failed trial ends on that wall. A smaller give-up means the attacker quits while the hub would still accept another block. A larger give-up still ends at 11, because the hub will not take a parent more than 10 blocks back.
      p(style="margin-bottom:0;")
        | The clock is simulated. The wait between blocks is random, and the average wait is the block time you set (10 seconds is the classroom default). The time column is that chain clock. This page does not mine on a live class session.

    .panel.panel-primary
      .panel-heading
        h2.panel-title Run a batch
      .panel-body
        form#attackSimForm
          .row
            .col-sm-6
              .form-group
                label(for="atkShares") Attacker hash share (%)
                input.form-control#atkShares(type="text" value="30, 45, 55, 70" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false")
                p.help-block One share, or several separated by commas. 30 means 30%. If every number is 1 or less, it is read as a fraction (0.55 = 55%).
            .col-sm-3
              .form-group
                label(for="atkBack") Blocks back (1–3)
                input.form-control#atkBack(type="number" min="1" max="3" step="1" value="2")
                p.help-block Where the private chain starts, behind the public tip.
            .col-sm-3
              .form-group
                label(for="atkTrials") Trials per share
                input.form-control#atkTrials(type="number" min="1" max="500" step="1" value="40")
                p.help-block Same start depth for every trial, so shares are comparable.
          .row
            .col-sm-3
              .form-group
                label(for="atkPreChain") Honest pre-chain length
                input.form-control#atkPreChain(type="number" min="1" max="100" step="1" value="10")
                p.help-block Public blocks before the attack starts. Must be at least the start depth.
            .col-sm-3
              .form-group
                label(for="atkBlockTime") Average block time (seconds)
                input.form-control#atkBlockTime(type="number" min="0.1" max="600" step="0.1" value="10")
                p.help-block Mean wait for the next block. The classroom uses 10s.
            .col-sm-3
              .form-group
                label(for="atkGiveUp") Give-up depth
                input.form-control#atkGiveUp(type="number" min="2" max="64" step="1" value="11")
                p.help-block Attacker stops this far behind. The lab’s stale-parent wall is 11.
            .col-sm-3
              .form-group
                label(for="atkSeed") Seed (optional)
                input.form-control#atkSeed(type="text" placeholder="blank = Math.random" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false")
                p.help-block Same seed replays the same block-by-block luck.
          button.btn.btn-primary.btn-lg#runBtn(type="submit") Run simulation
          p#simStatus(aria-live="polite")
          #simError.alert.alert-danger(style="display:none;margin-top:12px;" role="alert")

    #simResults(style="display:none;")
      .panel.panel-info
        .panel-heading
          h2.panel-title Win rate by hash share
        .panel-body
          p#resultNote.help-block(style="margin-bottom:12px;")
          .table-responsive
            table.table.table-striped
              thead
                tr
                  th(scope="col") Attacker share
                  th(scope="col") Trials
                  th(scope="col") Wins
                  th(scope="col") Failures
                  th(scope="col") Win rate
              tbody#summaryBody
          h3(style="font-size:15px;margin:18px 0 8px;") Win rate vs share
          #winChart.attack-chart(role="img" aria-label="Bar chart of win rate by attacker hash share")

      .panel.panel-default
        .panel-heading
          h2.panel-title Every trial
        .panel-body
          .attack-table-wrap
            table.table.table-striped
              thead
                tr
                  th(scope="col") #
                  th(scope="col") Attacker share
                  th(scope="col") Start depth
                  th(scope="col") Result
                  th(scope="col") Attacker / honest blocks
                  th(scope="col") Simulated time
                  th(scope="col") End reason
              tbody#trialBody
          details
            summary How to read a row
            p(style="margin:8px 0 0;")
              | Win means the attacker’s block became the hub’s canonical tip, listed as “Reorg at block N”. Fail means the public tip pulled that many blocks ahead of the private tip. At 11 behind, the next private block would be rejected as a stale parent, so the attacker cannot recover. A row that says Timed out hit the safety cap before either of those. The cap does not choose a winner. Block counts and the clock start when the race starts, after the honest pre-chain is already in place.

  script(src="/javascripts/lab/blockHash.js?v=hashfix1")
  script(src="/javascripts/network/RelayBlockchainState.js?v=p4fix15")
  script(src="/javascripts/lab/attackSim.js?v=attacksim3")
